    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0475" n="391" xml:id="pg391"/>

                <head>No. 197.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3, 1886</date>.
                        [Received July 6.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 29th of
                    May, I have the honor to inform you that I am instructed by the Earl of Rosebery
                    to state that the matters therein referred to will receive the careful attention
                    of Her Majesty’s Government after the necessary communication with the Dominion
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
